Replaced the linear scan with a lazily built 65536-entry direct lookup table, filled in reverse so duplicate message numbers still return the first matching entry. This makes each lookup O(1) instead of O(MESGS).

```include
#include <array>
```

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const auto table = []() {
        std::array<const Profile::MESG*, 65536> t{};
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            t[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        return t;
    }();

    return table[num];
}
```